Diet Planning Assistant with Persistence - Updated Logic Module (logic.py)
This updated version of logic.py incorporates database-backed conversation persistence using LangChain's SQLChatMessageHistory. It enables the chatbot to save, load, and switch between multiple chat sessions stored in a local SQLite database.

Key Changes & New Features
Database Integration: Utilizes SQLChatMessageHistory connected via sqlite:///conversations.db to persist message states across turns and application restarts.

Session Management:

_initialize_session() and _generate_session_id() dynamically create unique timestamped session IDs (e.g., Diet Chat - YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS).

new_session() starts a fresh conversation thread.

load_session() switches the active context to an existing chat session ID.

History Retrieval: Added get_messages() to fetch the message queue for the UI, and a static method get_previous_conversations() that queries the underlying SQLite database to list all stored sessions containing active dialogue.

